                    {
                        "sense_id": "44ba4d43-85fc-3ef5-83d1-274ed6a2667e",
                        "entry_id": "a5ca5b28-6778-36c5-a9e0-5b4cd4be06f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who stones."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "be20e08f-3841-40af-9744-9485016ce5c3",
                                "sense_id": "44ba4d43-85fc-3ef5-83d1-274ed6a2667e",
                                "text": "At eight you thought of boys as cat drowners and bird stoners. At nine there was another reason for boys' existence: they either noticed you or they didn't, and it desperately mattered which."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4759cc9f-70bf-3fed-bb6a-86524c791070",
                        "entry_id": "a5ca5b28-6778-36c5-a9e0-5b4cd4be06f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A machine to remove the stones (pits) from fruit."
